Problem: Boats to Save People (LC 881)

Pattern: Two Pointers + Sorting

Approach:

1. Sort the people by their weights.
2. Use two pointers, one at the lightest person and one at the heaviest person.
3. Initialize the number of boats as zero.
4. Check whether the lightest and heaviest people can fit in the same boat.
5. If they can fit, put both in the same boat and move both pointers inward.
6. If they cannot fit, the heaviest person must go alone, so move the right pointer inward.
7. Increase the boat count after each boat is used.
8. Continue until everyone has been placed in a boat.
9. Return the total number of boats.

Key Idea:
Always try to pair the heaviest person with the lightest person. If even they cannot fit together, the heaviest person must go alone.

Time Complexity: O(n log n)

Space Complexity: O(1) extra
